<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">International Students</div>
  <p>See page <span data-field="international_page_ref">{{ international_page_ref }}</span> for additional information.</p>

  <div class="subsection-title">Students in Western Regional Graduate Programs</div>
  <p>Students from <span data-field="region_1">{{ region_1 }}</span>, <span data-field="region_2">{{ region_2 }}</span>, <span data-field="region_3">{{ region_3 }}</span>, <span data-field="region_4">{{ region_4 }}</span>, <span data-field="region_5">{{ region_5 }}</span>, <span data-field="region_6">{{ region_6 }}</span>, <span data-field="region_7">{{ region_7 }}</span>, <span data-field="region_8">{{ region_8 }}</span>, <span data-field="region_9">{{ region_9 }}</span>, <span data-field="region_10">{{ region_10 }}</span>, <span data-field="region_11">{{ region_11 }}</span>, and <span data-field="region_12">{{ region_12 }}</span> may be eligible for resident tuition through the <span data-field="program_name">{{ program_name }}</span>. For international students, the Interstate Commission for Higher Education. This program is for students pursuing a graduate degree in clinical-community psychology, justice, northern studies or rural development. For more information about this program, contact the Graduate School at <span data-field="graduate_school_contact_email">{{ graduate_school_contact_email }}</span>, or online at <span data-field="graduate_school_contact_url">{{ graduate_school_contact_url }}</span>. Students with questions may also contact the <span data-field="admissions_contact_email">{{ admissions_contact_email }}</span>.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">Required Funding Amounts</div>
  <p>The minimum estimated cost for one school year at UAF for an international student is <span data-field="min_cost_international">{{ min_cost_international }}</span> for undergraduate students and <span data-field="min_cost_graduate">{{ min_cost_graduate }}</span> for graduate students. This covers university fees, room and board on campus, and a reasonable amount of personal expenses. It does not include transportation to and from Alaska, summer living or winter clothing costs. Add approximately <span data-field="additional_cost_amount">{{ additional_cost_amount }}</span> for summer living expenses.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">Transferring Credits</div>
  <p>Credit accepted at UAF that has been earned from other regionally accredited institutions, through military educational experiences, or credit accepted by special approval is considered transfer credit. Transfer credit is evaluated by the Office of Admissions and the Registrar and is subject to limitations within the University of Alaska System and Table 4 for transfer credits.</p>
  <p>For more information about transfer credits, see the Admissions Office of Admissions and the Registrar. For additional information about the SOC program, see <span data-field="soc_program_url">{{ soc_program_url }}</span>.</p>

  <div class="subsection-title">Transferring Credits Within the UAF System</div>
  <p>Transfer credits are evaluated by the Office of Admissions and the Registrar. Transfer credits are considered transfer credit if they have been earned from another regionally accredited institution. Transfer credits are considered transfer credit if they have been earned from another regionally accredited institution. Transfer credits are considered transfer credit if they have been earned from another regionally accredited institution.</p>
  <p>Transfer credits are considered transfer credit if they have been earned from another regionally accredited institution. Transfer credits are considered transfer credit if they have been earned from another regionally accredited institution.</p>

