<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">Transferring Credits</div>
  <p>In general, undergraduate credits earned at the 100 level or above at a University of Alaska institution will transfer to UAF. In addition, in order to serve students who transfer from other institutions, the Office of Admissions and the Registrar has identified fully transferable general education requirements for baccalaureate degree programs.</p>
  <p>This applies even if there is no direct matching course work. Transfer credits are evaluated by the Office of Admissions and the Registrar.</p>

  <div class="subsection-title">Credit for Language Testing</div>
  <p>UAF accepts successful test results from Brigham Young University or other national testing programs (subject to approval) for placement in language courses. The credit for 12 credits. The first 10 credits may be applied to the core curriculum language requirement. The remaining credits must be submitted directly to the Office of Admissions and the Registrar for review.</p>

  <div class="subsection-title">International Baccalaureate Diploma Program</div>
  <p>The International Baccalaureate Diploma Program is a two-year curriculum for students ages 16 to 19 and is similar to the final year of secondary school in Europe. UAF grants advanced credit, with a waiver of fees, for students who have completed the program. Students who have completed the program must submit an official copy of their IB exam results to the Office of Admissions and the Registrar.</p>
</div>

