<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <div class="section-title">CREDIT FOR PRIOR LEARNING</div>
      <p>The Academic Advising Center administers the credit for prior learning program, wherein students may earn undergraduate credit based on university-level learning they have obtained outside the university. Students can document their prior learning through a portfolio or copies of licenses and certificates earned. Certificates, associate or bachelor's degree students may earn credit for prior learning requirements through the credit for prior learning program.</p>
      <p>Credentials for admitted degree students who are currently enrolled are reviewed by faculty from participating departments. Students must make an appointment with an academic advisor to discuss the process and make recommendations for awarding prior learning credit. Review is based on equivalency to courses listed in this catalog. Credit received for prior learning does not affect your GPA and is not transferable to other institutions. Students must apply for transfer credit for specified national and state authorizations, including GED, CLEP, and AP. Students must apply for transfer credit for prior learning.</p>
      <p>For further information or assistance, contact the Academic Advising Center at 907-474-6396 or uaf.edu/advising/cpl.</p>

      <div class="sub-section-title">COMPETENCY TESTING</div>
      <p>Students with appropriate background experience may complete certain components of the UAF core curriculum via competency testing. Credit by exam is not available.</p>
      <div class="sub-section-title">Library Competency Exam</div>
      <p>The Library Competency Exam, administered by UAF Testing Services, is offered to fulfill the core curriculum requirement for L101X and L100X. The LCE, offered daily in Testing Services for $25, is designed to test or verify a student's knowledge of standard library functions, services and organization. While no credit is awarded for passing this exam, a score of at least 85 percent will fulfill the core curriculum requirement for L101X and L100X. Please contact Testing Services at 907-474-5278, uaf-testing-dept@alaska.edu or 211 Griening Building for more information.</p>
      <div class="sub-section-title">Computer Skills Placement Exam</div>
      <p>The Computer Skills Placement Exam, administered by UAF Testing Services, is offered to fulfill the degree requirement for AIS 101. The CSE, offered daily in Testing Services for $25, is designed to test or verify a student's knowledge of information technology and file management procedures; word processing (Word), spreadsheets (Excel), databases (Access) and presentation (PowerPoint) software. While no credit is awarded for passing this exam, a score of at least 70 percent will fulfill the degree requirement for AIS 101. Please contact Testing Services at 907-474-5278, uaf-testing-dept@alaska.edu or 211 Griening Building for more information.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <div class="section-title">Registration</div>
      <p>You must register and pay tuition and fees to attend classes and earn credit. Registration is held each semester on dates published in the academic calendar (see inside front cover for calendar). Details about procedures for registering classes are provided in the UAF registration guide, available at http://uafonline.alaska.edu or www.uaf.edu/register.</p>
      <p>The first day of instruction for all semester-length courses is the date indicated in the official semester academic calendar. Any other dates are subject to change.</p>
      <p>Financially responsible for payment of your tuition and fees. If you do not pay your tuition and fees by the due date, you may not be able to receive your grades or transcripts.</p>

