      <div class="sub-section-title">Adding, Dropping and Withdrawing from Classes</div>
      <p>Information about the add/drop process can also be found at http://uafonline.alaska.edu. In the registration guide at the Office of Admissions and the Registrar or at www.uaf.edu/register. Add, drops and withdrawals are subject to the deadlines listed in Table 8.</p>
      <p>Students are expected to begin attending classes on the first day of instruction. Some departments, in trying to find space for students on waitlists, require students to register for the class.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <div class="section-title">NONATTENDANCE DROP POLICY</div>
      <p>Students are expected to begin attending classes on the first day of instruction. Some departments, in trying to find space for students on waitlists, require students to register for the class.</p>
      <div class="sub-section-title">Faculty-Initiated Drop or Withdrawal</div>
      <p>Faculty-initiated drops or withdrawals are subject to the deadlines listed in Table 8. Faculty members have the right to drop students who do not meet course prerequisites, or who have not participated in class. Faculty-initiated withdrawals are subject to the deadlines listed in Table 8.</p>
      <div class="sub-section-title">Directed and Individual Study</div>
      <p>Directed study courses allow a student to contract with an instructor to enroll in an individual course that is listed in the catalog but in a semester in which the course is not offered.</p>
      <p>For example, a directed study proposal may be approved if the student wishes to study a topic that is not offered in the catalog. The student must submit a directed study proposal to the instructor and the Academic Advising Center for approval. The student must have an academic advisor's signature on the proposal.</p>
      <p>Individual study courses are not available via the web. To register for a directed or individual study course, the student must contact the instructor and the Office of Admissions and the Registrar.</p>
